10
00:00:51,971 --> 00:00:52,867
THIS DRAMA
IS A WORK OF FICTION

11
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:53,900
CHILD AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION

12
00:00:57,986 --> 00:00:59,988
ANY ADVICE FOR YOUNGER DESIGNERS
OR THOSE FINDING THEIR WAY?

13
00:01:00,989 --> 00:01:03,909
DON'T TRY TOO HARD TO CHANGE YOURSELF
CHANGE WHERE YOU ARE

14
00:01:08,955 --> 00:01:09,956
Mr. Kang.

15
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:12,083
Yes?

16
00:01:13,293 --> 00:01:14,294
What do you think

17
00:01:15,086 --> 00:01:18,590
about me applying
for that expat position to Paris?

18
00:01:29,309 --> 00:01:30,644
I was just asking.

19
00:01:31,102 --> 00:01:33,396
I'm already learning a lot right now

20
00:01:34,189 --> 00:01:37,400
but I was wondering what it'd be like
to be somewhere completely new.

21
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:42,822
I think it's a great idea.

22
00:01:45,825 --> 00:01:48,119
- Do you mean it?
- Of course.

23
00:01:48,912 --> 00:01:51,206
It's important to learn
in a different environment.

24
00:01:53,166 --> 00:01:55,710
And an employee's growth
is an advantage to the business.

25
00:01:57,212 --> 00:01:58,213
Give it a go.

26
00:02:02,133 --> 00:02:03,134
What about you?

27
00:02:04,177 --> 00:02:05,178
Me?

28
00:02:05,762 --> 00:02:06,763
Are you okay with it?

29
00:02:08,139 --> 00:02:09,140
Of course.

30
00:02:09,933 --> 00:02:12,477
The flight to Paris
isn't that long anyway.

31
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,531
What? Hey.

32
00:02:24,864 --> 00:02:26,074
Why would you go there?

33
00:02:26,157 --> 00:02:27,867
You just started dating
for the first time.

34
00:02:27,951 --> 00:02:28,952
What did he say?

35
00:02:29,286 --> 00:02:30,996
What do you think?
He must be shocked and scared.

36
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,581
He said he's fine with it.

37
00:02:33,373 --> 00:02:34,457
- What?
- What?

38
00:02:36,042 --> 00:02:37,919
He told me to go to Paris.

39
00:02:38,003 --> 00:02:40,171
Wait, maybe he was too flustered.

40
00:02:40,922 --> 00:02:42,048
He seemed to mean it.

41
00:02:43,383 --> 00:02:45,343
Hey, let me tell you this
because I've been there.

42
00:02:46,344 --> 00:02:48,179
Long-distance relationships
never work out.

43
00:02:49,222 --> 00:02:51,182
- Why?
- Your boyfriend

44
00:02:51,391 --> 00:02:53,393
is someone even CEO Han Jeong-yeon
wanted to date.

45
00:02:53,476 --> 00:02:55,562
Women won't let him be alone
during that long period.

46
00:02:55,979 --> 00:02:57,397
- They'll snatch him right away.
- What?

47
00:02:57,480 --> 00:02:59,691
Yes, you said there were
more than a couple of women

48
00:02:59,774 --> 00:03:01,318
who asked him out at work.

49
00:03:02,902 --> 00:03:03,903
LET'S SNATCH KANG HA-GI RIGHT AWAY

50
00:03:03,987 --> 00:03:05,905
<i>- Kang Ha-gi!
- Kang Ha-gi!</i>

51
00:03:05,989 --> 00:03:07,032
No way.

52
00:03:07,115 --> 00:03:09,117
No matter how I think about it,
it can't happen.

53
00:03:27,510 --> 00:03:28,970
<i>I love you, Da-reum.</i>

54
00:03:29,846 --> 00:03:31,056
<i>I love you, too.</i>

55
00:03:38,438 --> 00:03:39,564
- Hey!
- My goodness!

56
00:03:40,106 --> 00:03:41,149
What's taking you so long?

57
00:03:41,691 --> 00:03:42,817
I'm hungry.

58
00:03:42,901 --> 00:03:45,153
You've been
frying those dumplings all day long.

59
00:03:45,236 --> 00:03:46,279
Why, that...

60
00:03:55,747 --> 00:03:57,040
Yes.

61
00:03:59,209 --> 00:04:01,753
Wow, you've burned them all.

62
00:04:02,671 --> 00:04:06,049
So why did you tell her to go
if you didn't even mean it?

63
00:04:07,550 --> 00:04:09,344
It's so hot.

64
00:04:12,639 --> 00:04:13,640
Listen up.

65
00:04:13,723 --> 00:04:14,766
Dating is like a fried dumpling.

66
00:04:15,934 --> 00:04:17,394
When it gets hot, flip it over.

67
00:04:17,477 --> 00:04:19,062
When you want to cool it,
put it down.

68
00:04:19,437 --> 00:04:22,524
You need a bit of distance
to stay together even longer.

69
00:04:22,982 --> 00:04:25,026
You're taking a step back
to take two steps forward later.

70
00:04:25,110 --> 00:04:27,404
That's what real players do.

71
00:04:32,534 --> 00:04:34,285
Why did it have to be France?

72
00:04:35,203 --> 00:04:38,039
People there greet each other
with a kiss on the cheek.

73
00:04:39,249 --> 00:04:41,334
- I don't like it.
- Are you anxious already?

74
00:04:42,711 --> 00:04:44,838
- I'm not.
- You're scared.

75
00:04:44,921 --> 00:04:48,216
Just be cool and let Da-reum go.
Don't be so lame.

76
00:04:48,967 --> 00:04:51,678
If you go, that'll be the end of it.
You two will break up for sure.

77
00:04:52,095 --> 00:04:53,471
Let her go
so you can be together longer.

78
00:04:53,555 --> 00:04:55,223
Be cool about it and let her go.
It's a go!

79
00:04:55,306 --> 00:04:57,058
You cannot go. It's a no!

80
00:04:58,143 --> 00:04:59,894
- Go!
- No!

81
00:04:59,978 --> 00:05:01,855
- Go!
- No!

82
00:05:05,817 --> 00:05:07,527
{\an8}FINAL EPISODE

83
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:08,778
{\an8}CEO KANG HA-GI

84
00:05:16,911 --> 00:05:18,079
{\an8}Come in.

85
00:05:19,372 --> 00:05:20,457
{\an8}Mr. Kang.

86
00:05:21,291 --> 00:05:23,293
{\an8}Have you seen the notice
HAN sent today?

87
00:05:24,252 --> 00:05:25,336
{\an8}No, not yet.

88
00:05:25,754 --> 00:05:27,881
{\an8}It was about our expat employee.

89
00:05:28,548 --> 00:05:32,385
{\an8}"If possible, we'd like to have
Ms. Nam Da-reum sent here."

90
00:05:32,969 --> 00:05:34,220
{\an8}That's what it says.

91
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,934
REQUESTING EXPAT EMPLOYEE FROM KOREA

92
00:05:40,018 --> 00:05:41,227
STATIONED AT:
MAISON HAN PARIS HEADQUARTERS

93
00:05:41,311 --> 00:05:42,437
REQUESTED EMPLOYEE:
NAM DA-REUM

94
00:05:43,146 --> 00:05:45,190
I haven't checked
with Ms. Da-reum yet.

95
00:05:46,274 --> 00:05:48,568
- Please do.
- Sorry?

96
00:05:49,486 --> 00:05:51,988
Tell them that we'll consider
the request favorably

97
00:05:52,071 --> 00:05:53,656
if she wishes to go.

98
00:05:55,533 --> 00:05:57,827
- Favorably?
- Yes.

99
00:05:58,286 --> 00:05:59,329
It's a great opportunity.

100
00:05:59,788 --> 00:06:01,915
The employee's growth leads
to the company's growth.

101
00:06:03,333 --> 00:06:04,459
It's growth for everyone.

102
00:06:04,542 --> 00:06:06,377
GROWTH FOR EVERYONE

103
00:06:09,214 --> 00:06:10,548
Mr. Kang.

104
00:06:10,965 --> 00:06:14,219
- Are you sure about this?
- Yes, of course.

105
00:06:17,138 --> 00:06:18,181
All right, then.

106
00:06:43,373 --> 00:06:44,374
KIM MIN-WOO

107
00:06:44,666 --> 00:06:47,293
<i>Hey, I just saw
Mr. Choi Seong-wook here.</i>

108
00:06:53,007 --> 00:06:55,176
HAND CAR WASH

109
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:57,095
It'll take you forever
to wash all three cars.

110
00:06:57,178 --> 00:06:58,471
Move it, will you?

111
00:06:58,847 --> 00:07:00,056
Did you get this part?

112
00:07:00,139 --> 00:07:03,059
You didn't get the wheels.
Get to it already.

113
00:07:04,269 --> 00:07:05,562
- Choi.
- Yes?

114
00:07:05,645 --> 00:07:07,814
Don't just wipe the sides.
Get the roof too.

115
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:09,190
Yes, sir.

116
00:07:10,483 --> 00:07:14,487
- Don't slack off. Wipe it harder.
- Yes, sir.

117
00:07:49,355 --> 00:07:50,565
You left to do this job?

118
00:07:50,773 --> 00:07:52,567
Why did you do it
when you didn't even make a big haul?

119
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:56,237
Right? Tell me about it.

120
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,745
Why didn't you send them

121
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:05,455
the final version?

122
00:08:10,668 --> 00:08:11,753
Because I'm an idiot.

123
00:08:19,594 --> 00:08:20,762
I couldn't bear

124
00:08:21,471 --> 00:08:22,847
to see you go down.

125
00:08:27,644 --> 00:08:28,645
Do you remember?

126
00:08:29,729 --> 00:08:33,441
When we first got
an office for Appello

127
00:08:34,442 --> 00:08:36,277
we carried boxes
all throughout the night.

128
00:08:37,528 --> 00:08:38,821
Whenever the server crashed

129
00:08:38,905 --> 00:08:40,865
we'd spend days
practically living there.

130
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:43,660
So how could I

131
00:08:44,994 --> 00:08:46,371
forget all that?

132
00:08:50,875 --> 00:08:53,628
I got some relief
after doing that awful thing.

133
00:08:55,338 --> 00:08:57,131
But my heart hit rock bottom.

134
00:08:58,466 --> 00:08:59,550
I didn't know what got into me.

135
00:09:03,221 --> 00:09:04,514
This is for the better.

136
00:09:08,184 --> 00:09:09,394
No one's going to understand that.

137
00:09:10,979 --> 00:09:12,897
You should've stabbed my back
and gotten good money for it.

138
00:09:14,357 --> 00:09:15,441
I still...

139
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:20,446
despise you so much.

140
00:09:24,492 --> 00:09:26,411
Yes, that's only fair.

141
00:09:33,751 --> 00:09:34,794
Ha-gi.

142
00:09:37,213 --> 00:09:38,256
It's not your fault

143
00:09:39,424 --> 00:09:42,301
that I've become broken.
It's not because you succeeded.

144
00:09:44,262 --> 00:09:45,263
It's just that...

145
00:09:49,183 --> 00:09:52,437
Instead of cheering you on

146
00:09:54,397 --> 00:09:57,150
I hated myself for feeling so petty.

147
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,030
And I couldn't deal with it.

148
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,955
I'm sorry. I mean it.

149
00:10:15,168 --> 00:10:16,461
And thanks

150
00:10:17,128 --> 00:10:20,465
for giving me a chance
to make an excuse.

151
00:10:24,677 --> 00:10:27,263
Hey, Choi. We're busy over here!

152
00:10:27,889 --> 00:10:28,973
Yes, coming!

153
00:10:37,356 --> 00:10:38,357
Hey, Ha-gi.

154
00:10:40,985 --> 00:10:42,153
I'll always be...

155
00:10:43,738 --> 00:10:45,573
grateful for you, man.

156
00:10:48,951 --> 00:10:49,994
I have to go.

157
00:11:17,772 --> 00:11:19,357
OVERSEAS ASSIGNMENT APPLICATION

158
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:21,109
ASSIGNED TO:
MAISON HAN PARIS HEADQUARTERS

159
00:11:26,864 --> 00:11:28,324
I thought you'd be thrilled.

160
00:11:31,744 --> 00:11:33,913
What's wrong? Is it Mr. Kang?

161
00:11:41,963 --> 00:11:44,507
He's already having a tough time
because of Mr. Choi.

162
00:11:45,174 --> 00:11:47,260
I didn't want to add to that.

163
00:11:50,096 --> 00:11:52,807
Well, I guess
the timing is a bit off.

164
00:11:53,724 --> 00:11:54,725
Will you be okay...

165
00:11:56,894 --> 00:11:58,187
giving up on this?

166
00:12:03,317 --> 00:12:08,072
You should give serious thought
about what you really want.

167
00:12:25,298 --> 00:12:26,674
Seong-wook said

168
00:12:27,592 --> 00:12:29,051
he hated himself
for having awful feelings

169
00:12:29,135 --> 00:12:31,137
for someone
he should be showing support to.

170
00:12:34,891 --> 00:12:36,058
It hit close to home.

171
00:12:38,978 --> 00:12:41,480
I know it's a great opportunity
for Ms. Da-reum.

172
00:12:44,901 --> 00:12:46,319
But I want her to stay.

173
00:12:49,572 --> 00:12:50,781
I find myself so pathetic.

174
00:12:54,452 --> 00:12:56,162
By now, I should be
used to saying goodbye...

175
00:13:00,625 --> 00:13:02,168
to people.

176
00:13:04,712 --> 00:13:06,047
But it's too hard.

177
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,802
Then cling to her.

178
00:13:12,845 --> 00:13:13,888
Okay?

179
00:13:13,971 --> 00:13:15,723
If I did that
because I couldn't handle it

180
00:13:16,766 --> 00:13:18,559
it would kill her dream too.

181
00:13:19,185 --> 00:13:20,228
Wow.

182
00:13:22,813 --> 00:13:23,940
I should let her go.

183
00:13:29,737 --> 00:13:30,905
That's the right thing to do.

184
00:13:35,910 --> 00:13:37,286
I really can't deal with you.

185
00:13:47,255 --> 00:13:48,923
Hey, be careful.

186
00:13:49,715 --> 00:13:51,717
Hey, man. Pull it together.

187
00:13:51,801 --> 00:13:53,594
Kang Ha-gi.

188
00:13:53,970 --> 00:13:55,596
Hey, I'm fine.

189
00:13:55,930 --> 00:13:57,139
I'm totally fine.

190
00:13:57,682 --> 00:13:58,766
Let's go for round two.

191
00:13:59,558 --> 00:14:00,685
To my place!

192
00:14:01,936 --> 00:14:04,105
You have to give her
your drunken honesty

193
00:14:04,188 --> 00:14:05,856
- instead of looking wasted.
- Excellent.

194
00:14:07,566 --> 00:14:08,609
On my way.

195
00:14:08,985 --> 00:14:10,736
- My drunken confession!
- Okay.

196
00:14:10,820 --> 00:14:12,405
- On my way!
- Mr. Kang.

197
00:14:12,738 --> 00:14:13,823
Mr. Kang.

198
00:14:19,870 --> 00:14:21,664
- Are you okay?
- It's Ms. Da-reum.

199
00:14:22,123 --> 00:14:23,207
It's me.

200
00:14:23,749 --> 00:14:25,543
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

201
00:14:25,668 --> 00:14:26,711
Ms. Da-reum.

202
00:14:30,047 --> 00:14:31,340
You're so cute.

203
00:14:33,843 --> 00:14:35,928
You're way too cute, my dear Da-reum.

204
00:14:38,889 --> 00:14:40,141
So you're drunk.

205
00:14:42,893 --> 00:14:44,854
How do I let you go
when you're so cute?

206
00:14:48,399 --> 00:14:49,525
Kiss me.

207
00:14:52,528 --> 00:14:54,238
Have you lost your mind?

208
00:14:54,322 --> 00:14:55,614
Go do that at home.

209
00:14:55,698 --> 00:14:57,074
Mr. Kang.

210
00:14:57,283 --> 00:14:58,659
Are you okay?

211
00:14:58,743 --> 00:15:00,494
I've never seen him so wasted before.

212
00:15:02,788 --> 00:15:04,707
Let's take him back home for now.

213
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:06,625
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

214
00:15:07,585 --> 00:15:10,087
- Are you okay?
- Someone hit me.

215
00:15:10,171 --> 00:15:12,006
- No one did. Let's go.
- No.

216
00:15:13,466 --> 00:15:15,051
Why did you drink so much?

217
00:15:15,593 --> 00:15:16,761
You can go too.

218
00:15:17,011 --> 00:15:20,222
- I'm fine, really.
- Where are you telling me to go?

219
00:15:21,474 --> 00:15:22,892
Sit down for a minute.

220
00:15:43,537 --> 00:15:44,538
Mr. Kang?

221
00:15:45,831 --> 00:15:46,832
Mr. Kang.

222
00:16:01,097 --> 00:16:02,515
Don't go.

223
00:16:10,606 --> 00:16:12,441
Don't go, Da-reum.

224
00:16:38,717 --> 00:16:40,845
<i>He's not cool with it.</i>

225
00:16:41,971 --> 00:16:44,765
<i>He just doesn't want
to get in your way.</i>

226
00:17:17,506 --> 00:17:20,342
{\an8}CONTACT SOLUTION, Q-TIPS

227
00:17:21,135 --> 00:17:23,929
{\an8}TRAVEL PILLOW, BLANKET,
PAIN RELIEF PATCHES, <i>RAMYEON</i>

228
00:17:35,357 --> 00:17:36,859
OUR BELOVED
PARIS, FRANCE

229
00:17:36,942 --> 00:17:38,444
{\an8}SUPPLIES FOR PARIS

230
00:17:38,527 --> 00:17:39,904
BAND-AID, OINTMENT, INSTANT SOUP

231
00:18:03,802 --> 00:18:05,471
Should we do these

232
00:18:05,554 --> 00:18:08,098
for Olivier's new colors?

233
00:18:09,225 --> 00:18:10,643
It's too light.

234
00:18:10,726 --> 00:18:12,561
Wasn't there a jacket?

235
00:18:12,645 --> 00:18:13,646
Like this one.

236
00:18:15,105 --> 00:18:16,941
<i>Ms. Da-reum took the day off.</i>

237
00:18:17,024 --> 00:18:20,110
<i>Today was the deadline to apply
to work abroad, and she didn't apply.</i>

238
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:39,630
SPICY CHICKEN, ANGUK BRANCH
8,530 WON, ACCEPT

239
00:18:56,605 --> 00:18:58,649
QUICK DELIVERY

240
00:19:02,903 --> 00:19:06,073
{\an8}ONE, TWO, THREE, FOUR, FIVE
LET'S GO

241
00:19:06,156 --> 00:19:09,201
<i>- D.N.X.
- D.N.X.</i>

242
00:19:09,285 --> 00:19:10,869
<i>- D.N.X.
- D.N.X.</i>

243
00:19:10,953 --> 00:19:12,121
MUSIC WAVE

244
00:19:12,204 --> 00:19:16,292
- D.N.X.
- D.N.X.

245
00:19:20,129 --> 00:19:21,630
- One.
- Two.

246
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:23,257
- Three.
- Four.

247
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,009
Five. Let's go!

248
00:19:25,092 --> 00:19:26,510
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

249
00:19:34,101 --> 00:19:36,729
{\an8}ONE, TWO,
THREE, FOUR

250
00:19:36,812 --> 00:19:39,690
FIVE, LET'S GO

251
00:19:55,372 --> 00:19:59,126
I feel so much more relieved
after deciding not to go.

252
00:20:06,383 --> 00:20:09,011
I mean, Paris isn't a big deal.

253
00:20:09,386 --> 00:20:12,306
Here, I got my friends, Appello...

254
00:20:13,766 --> 00:20:15,643
<i>No matter how hard things get</i>

255
00:20:16,852 --> 00:20:17,978
don't let go of my hand.

256
00:20:20,522 --> 00:20:21,523
Okay.

257
00:20:24,818 --> 00:20:26,153
...and Mr. Kang.

258
00:20:29,990 --> 00:20:31,283
Okay, Nam Da-reum.

259
00:20:31,992 --> 00:20:33,077
You made a great decision.

260
00:20:42,294 --> 00:20:43,295
How sweet.

261
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:13,867
You're alive.

262
00:21:18,122 --> 00:21:19,164
Chan.

263
00:21:24,795 --> 00:21:26,797
I should've been there by your side.

264
00:21:28,006 --> 00:21:29,091
I'm sorry.

265
00:21:30,592 --> 00:21:31,635
Why are you apologizing?

266
00:21:34,638 --> 00:21:35,848
I let go of your hand.

267
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:39,518
You didn't.

268
00:21:40,686 --> 00:21:41,937
I'm the one who ran away.

269
00:21:48,986 --> 00:21:52,322
Jeez. You must've been
the most frightened.

270
00:21:53,157 --> 00:21:55,868
But I must've been young too
because I ran away like you.

271
00:22:00,664 --> 00:22:01,665
Let us...

272
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:04,877
stop running away.

273
00:22:07,463 --> 00:22:08,547
Come back, Roy.

274
00:22:13,051 --> 00:22:15,596
Do you think
the other guys will accept me?

275
00:22:20,017 --> 00:22:23,520
They talk crap about you
when your part comes on at practice.

276
00:22:24,688 --> 00:22:26,607
They pretend like
they hate you so much

277
00:22:27,149 --> 00:22:28,192
yet they wait.

278
00:22:32,821 --> 00:22:33,864
Did you see the ad?

279
00:22:34,865 --> 00:22:36,533
That's how we all feel.

280
00:23:00,265 --> 00:23:01,600
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

281
00:23:03,268 --> 00:23:05,020
<i>You know the application
is due today, right?</i>

282
00:23:05,646 --> 00:23:06,980
<i>I'll wait until you come.</i>

283
00:23:21,662 --> 00:23:24,456
YOU KNOW THE APPLICATION
IS DUE TODAY, RIGHT?

284
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:25,666
I'LL WAIT UNTIL YOU COME

285
00:23:59,116 --> 00:24:00,117
Ms. Da-reum.

286
00:24:01,535 --> 00:24:02,828
Have you really been waiting for me?

287
00:24:04,454 --> 00:24:05,455
Yes.

288
00:24:10,711 --> 00:24:12,045
You didn't turn in the application...

289
00:24:14,047 --> 00:24:15,549
and you made me worry all day.

290
00:24:18,010 --> 00:24:21,221
You kept pretending
like you were cool with it too.

291
00:24:21,805 --> 00:24:23,140
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

292
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,309
I'm the expert at acting fine.

293
00:24:27,352 --> 00:24:28,854
Is that why you ran away?

294
00:24:33,233 --> 00:24:34,234
No.

295
00:24:36,987 --> 00:24:39,364
Working with you

296
00:24:39,990 --> 00:24:41,199
eating with you

297
00:24:41,909 --> 00:24:44,536
and staying by your side
on days when we have nothing to do

298
00:24:45,704 --> 00:24:47,205
were what I loved.

299
00:24:51,793 --> 00:24:54,046
So I wanted to keep being with you.

300
00:24:56,506 --> 00:24:57,507
Ms. Da-reum.

301
00:24:58,008 --> 00:24:59,718
If I must choose one or the other...

302
00:25:01,970 --> 00:25:03,096
I choose you.

303
00:25:16,026 --> 00:25:17,110
You're right.

304
00:25:17,819 --> 00:25:19,488
I didn't want you to go.

305
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:25,118
I thought this could mean
goodbye forever

306
00:25:26,370 --> 00:25:27,454
so I got anxious.

307
00:25:29,665 --> 00:25:31,083
But what beat my anxiety...

308
00:25:35,253 --> 00:25:37,297
must be my love for you.

309
00:25:38,966 --> 00:25:40,300
What I hated more was the idea

310
00:25:41,176 --> 00:25:42,219
of you not going because of me.

311
00:25:46,848 --> 00:25:48,100
When you talked about Paris

312
00:25:49,851 --> 00:25:51,603
your eyes dazzled so brightly.

313
00:25:53,981 --> 00:25:55,607
It was the face...

314
00:25:58,026 --> 00:25:59,277
I fell in love with.

315
00:26:00,904 --> 00:26:01,947
A face full of excitement

316
00:26:02,614 --> 00:26:03,740
and happiness.

317
00:26:05,325 --> 00:26:06,702
I hope to see you...

318
00:26:09,079 --> 00:26:11,123
always looking like that.

319
00:26:19,256 --> 00:26:20,841
Don't worry about me and go.

320
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:22,843
See and experience

321
00:26:23,969 --> 00:26:25,053
as much as you can.

322
00:26:29,057 --> 00:26:30,600
So that you can do an even better job

323
00:26:31,476 --> 00:26:33,937
at what you want to do, okay?

324
00:26:40,235 --> 00:26:41,486
Even if I leave...

325
00:26:45,157 --> 00:26:46,908
you won't let go, will you?

326
00:26:49,619 --> 00:26:50,787
Of course not.

327
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:53,498
We'd be holding each other
more tightly.

328
00:26:57,252 --> 00:26:58,253
Let us

329
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,047
trust each other.

330
00:27:06,428 --> 00:27:07,471
Okay?

331
00:27:30,619 --> 00:27:32,204
Congratulations, Da-reum.

332
00:27:32,287 --> 00:27:34,581
I mean, Paris? That's so cool.

333
00:27:35,248 --> 00:27:37,125
Upload lots of pictures
in the group chat, okay?

334
00:27:37,209 --> 00:27:39,086
And you have to come back.

335
00:27:39,169 --> 00:27:41,505
Yes, I'll make sure
I check in with you.

336
00:27:41,588 --> 00:27:43,381
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

337
00:27:43,465 --> 00:27:45,759
Wait, you can't do that without me.
Let me do it too.

338
00:27:45,842 --> 00:27:48,053
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

339
00:27:48,136 --> 00:27:49,471
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

340
00:27:54,101 --> 00:27:55,393
Are you ready to go?

341
00:27:55,852 --> 00:27:58,897
I have something to share with you.

342
00:28:04,569 --> 00:28:07,114
Oh my gosh. Mr. Kang.

343
00:28:09,241 --> 00:28:10,242
Actually...

344
00:28:12,452 --> 00:28:13,578
Ms. Da-reum and I are...

345
00:28:14,496 --> 00:28:15,747
We know, Mr. Kang.

346
00:28:18,625 --> 00:28:20,627
Wow, congratulations.

347
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:22,129
- Congrats.
- Good for you.

348
00:28:22,212 --> 00:28:23,630
- Finally.
- It was about time.

349
00:28:26,508 --> 00:28:29,094
I wasn't done talking.

350
00:28:29,177 --> 00:28:32,639
Do you know how tiring it was
to pretend like we didn't know?

351
00:28:32,764 --> 00:28:36,768
- Tell me about it. It was tiring.
- So exhausting.

352
00:28:36,852 --> 00:28:38,562
It was fun to see your awful acting.

353
00:28:43,859 --> 00:28:46,403
We won't be able to hold
the rookies' meet-up for a while.

354
00:28:46,486 --> 00:28:47,571
Right?

355
00:28:47,654 --> 00:28:50,740
It was mostly the two of us, anyway.

356
00:28:52,826 --> 00:28:54,327
I need cola.

357
00:28:55,078 --> 00:28:57,080
Hey, give me some soda.

358
00:28:57,789 --> 00:28:58,915
That wrong message in the chat...

359
00:28:58,999 --> 00:29:00,292
Mr. Kang.

360
00:29:07,215 --> 00:29:09,176
- One, two, three, four.
- One, two, three, four.

361
00:29:09,259 --> 00:29:11,136
- Five, six, seven, eight.
- Five, six, seven, eight.

362
00:29:11,219 --> 00:29:13,555
- Two, two, three, four...
- Wait.

363
00:29:13,638 --> 00:29:15,932
Chan, you stepped out
half a beat too early.

364
00:29:16,016 --> 00:29:18,852
No, I stepped out at "two, two."
You got out at "two."

365
00:29:18,935 --> 00:29:20,061
You were both rushing.

366
00:29:20,145 --> 00:29:22,189
- Hey.
- You were both wrong, so get back.

367
00:29:22,272 --> 00:29:24,691
- Hey, Teo.
- Fine. I was wrong. Do it over.

368
00:29:24,774 --> 00:29:27,402
You know how it goes.
This isn't it. Hurry up.

369
00:29:32,616 --> 00:29:33,617
You're here.

370
00:29:40,457 --> 00:29:42,375
I'm a bit late, aren't I?

371
00:29:53,011 --> 00:29:54,638
I've been waiting for so long.

372
00:30:01,811 --> 00:30:04,022
- I missed you, kid.
- Me too.

373
00:30:04,105 --> 00:30:06,650
- Let me see our baby's face.
- Have you all been well?

374
00:30:06,733 --> 00:30:08,985
What did you go through?
You're a mess for a K-pop idol.

375
00:30:09,069 --> 00:30:10,904
- You're right.
- He looks way better than you guys.

376
00:30:10,987 --> 00:30:12,364
What are you talking about?

377
00:30:23,083 --> 00:30:24,668
- What took you so long?
- What took you so long?

378
00:30:27,087 --> 00:30:30,340
{\an8}APPELLO CLOSED
COLLEGEIST POP-UP IS OVER, THANK YOU

379
00:30:55,448 --> 00:30:56,825
Can you play this song?

380
00:31:12,966 --> 00:31:14,718
YOU
DEMO VERSION

381
00:31:20,682 --> 00:31:21,683
What do you think?

382
00:31:24,436 --> 00:31:25,437
I love it.

383
00:31:27,439 --> 00:31:28,481
That's it?

384
00:31:33,069 --> 00:31:34,070
It feels weird.

385
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:37,032
You may be saying it to your fans

386
00:31:37,699 --> 00:31:40,243
but it's what I wanted to say to you.

387
00:31:44,497 --> 00:31:45,582
So you're saying

388
00:31:46,958 --> 00:31:48,084
it's a pass?

389
00:31:59,346 --> 00:32:01,681
We both held out
for quite a long time.

390
00:32:04,934 --> 00:32:06,644
Hey, that's...

391
00:32:11,232 --> 00:32:14,903
This is the exact shape
that my all-time favorite celebrity

392
00:32:14,986 --> 00:32:16,696
always draws
when he signs autographs.

393
00:32:16,905 --> 00:32:18,656
Today is my birthday

394
00:32:18,740 --> 00:32:20,533
so I want to buy it for myself
as a gift.

395
00:32:20,784 --> 00:32:23,119
Excuse me. Happy birthday.

396
00:32:28,375 --> 00:32:29,459
<i>It was me.</i>

397
00:32:30,210 --> 00:32:31,920
I gave you that pendant
on your birthday.

398
00:32:36,966 --> 00:32:38,843
And because you had kept it all along

399
00:32:39,886 --> 00:32:41,721
I found the courage
to get back on stage.

400
00:32:45,725 --> 00:32:48,645
I also endured life,
believing that it was from you.

401
00:32:56,236 --> 00:32:57,278
I think...

402
00:32:59,114 --> 00:33:02,617
I figured out
what it is that I want to do.

403
00:33:03,868 --> 00:33:06,079
Just as I was happy as your fan

404
00:33:06,329 --> 00:33:10,083
I also want to do something
that'll awaken passion

405
00:33:10,750 --> 00:33:11,835
in people's hearts.

406
00:33:16,965 --> 00:33:18,383
Is that why you're going to Paris?

407
00:33:20,760 --> 00:33:21,803
Yes.

408
00:33:22,887 --> 00:33:24,431
I don't know
if I can pull it off, though.

409
00:33:25,181 --> 00:33:26,433
I'm sure you will.

410
00:33:27,350 --> 00:33:30,311
I've seen
how serious you are about this.

411
00:33:35,275 --> 00:33:38,153
I was happy to have someone
so wonderful as my fan.

412
00:33:43,658 --> 00:33:44,701
Now, it's your turn

413
00:33:45,869 --> 00:33:46,995
to do what makes your heart race.

414
00:34:05,466 --> 00:34:06,509
Passport.

415
00:34:06,926 --> 00:34:07,927
Here.

416
00:34:08,845 --> 00:34:09,846
The guidebook.

417
00:34:10,721 --> 00:34:11,764
Here.

418
00:34:12,807 --> 00:34:13,850
Emergency medicine.

419
00:34:16,102 --> 00:34:18,104
You basically bought me a pharmacy.

420
00:34:20,398 --> 00:34:21,732
Are you sure it's enough?

421
00:34:23,860 --> 00:34:25,194
I'm not going to Paris
to sell medicine.

422
00:34:25,820 --> 00:34:27,155
I just don't want you to get sick.

423
00:34:31,242 --> 00:34:33,619
I think I got everything, right?

424
00:34:43,296 --> 00:34:44,547
That's our knot.

425
00:34:45,173 --> 00:34:46,424
You attached it there.

426
00:34:49,677 --> 00:34:51,179
I'm taking this with me.

427
00:34:51,512 --> 00:34:53,264
So it'll feel like
we're still together.

428
00:35:04,192 --> 00:35:05,276
Are you touched?

429
00:35:08,571 --> 00:35:10,406
- A little.
- Only a little?

430
00:35:13,117 --> 00:35:14,118
Actually, a lot.

431
00:35:20,041 --> 00:35:21,876
Maybe I should leave
something behind too.

432
00:35:23,419 --> 00:35:24,420
Like what?

433
00:35:25,922 --> 00:35:27,840
It's a secret. I'll tell you later.

434
00:35:42,271 --> 00:35:43,606
I'll be back soon.

435
00:35:45,900 --> 00:35:47,235
I'll be waiting.

436
00:36:10,132 --> 00:36:13,261
DA-REUM HEART HA-GI

437
00:36:16,472 --> 00:36:19,809
6 MONTHS LATER

438
00:36:21,602 --> 00:36:22,979
Da-reum.

439
00:36:23,062 --> 00:36:25,022
The CEO wants this version
by three o'clock.

440
00:36:25,648 --> 00:36:27,567
By three o'clock today?

441
00:36:27,984 --> 00:36:29,735
Yes, that's her style.

442
00:36:31,821 --> 00:36:33,739
She's obviously Korean.

443
00:36:34,198 --> 00:36:35,199
You can do it.

444
00:36:35,866 --> 00:36:36,909
Can you?

445
00:36:38,869 --> 00:36:40,955
- I can.
- Yes.

446
00:37:08,941 --> 00:37:10,067
HAN AND KOREA

447
00:37:20,453 --> 00:37:21,871
Finally.

448
00:38:05,706 --> 00:38:07,958
<i>Ha-gi's mission while waiting.</i>

449
00:38:08,042 --> 00:38:09,126
<i>Sunlight.</i>

450
00:38:09,210 --> 00:38:12,004
<i>Water, then open the window
for some sunlight.</i>

451
00:38:12,380 --> 00:38:14,757
<i>When a new leaf grows,
send me a selfie with it.</i>

452
00:38:15,216 --> 00:38:18,427
<i>When a bud appears,
video call and show me.</i>

453
00:38:45,246 --> 00:38:46,747
- Bye.
- Bye.

454
00:38:59,760 --> 00:39:01,095
<i>Bonjour.</i>

455
00:39:02,763 --> 00:39:04,306
<i>Are you at work on the weekend?</i>

456
00:39:06,142 --> 00:39:07,351
Exactly.

457
00:39:07,893 --> 00:39:10,312
Ms. Han is no joke.

458
00:39:10,396 --> 00:39:12,064
She bombards me with work.

459
00:39:12,481 --> 00:39:13,816
She's worse than you.

460
00:39:13,983 --> 00:39:15,943
But why do you look excited?

461
00:39:18,028 --> 00:39:20,322
<i>It's tough, but it's still fun.</i>

462
00:39:20,990 --> 00:39:22,533
If you're enjoying it
even though it's tough

463
00:39:22,992 --> 00:39:24,034
that means you're good at it.

464
00:39:26,495 --> 00:39:27,997
You sound like a CEO.

465
00:39:28,581 --> 00:39:29,665
Because I am one.

466
00:39:33,085 --> 00:39:35,337
How's work? Is everything okay?

467
00:39:35,588 --> 00:39:37,548
<i>Oh, I found out just yesterday.</i>

468
00:39:37,631 --> 00:39:39,341
Mr. Young-woo and Ms. Min-a
are going out.

469
00:39:39,425 --> 00:39:40,468
<i>Really?</i>

470
00:39:41,051 --> 00:39:43,554
Oh, I knew it.

471
00:39:43,637 --> 00:39:45,931
- Since when?
- Since last week.

472
00:39:46,557 --> 00:39:49,351
That's crazy. How did you know?

473
00:39:49,685 --> 00:39:51,145
It was obvious.

474
00:39:51,353 --> 00:39:52,688
<i>Only those two think
it's still a secret.</i>

475
00:39:55,524 --> 00:39:56,776
We were the same.

476
00:39:59,737 --> 00:40:01,655
<i>Oh, right. Check this out.</i>

477
00:40:03,073 --> 00:40:04,241
I think it's going to bloom soon.

478
00:40:04,325 --> 00:40:06,243
Oh, that's so pretty.

479
00:40:06,577 --> 00:40:08,454
<i>How are you so good
at growing plants?</i>

480
00:40:08,537 --> 00:40:09,955
<i>I always end up killing them.</i>

481
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:12,291
- Are you grateful?
- Yes.

482
00:40:14,001 --> 00:40:15,085
Give me a reward.

483
00:40:23,636 --> 00:40:24,678
I miss you.

484
00:40:25,262 --> 00:40:26,263
<i>I miss you too.</i>

485
00:40:32,561 --> 00:40:34,814
Da-reum will come
to the concert on her own.

486
00:40:34,897 --> 00:40:36,190
You can ride with me.

487
00:40:37,107 --> 00:40:38,943
How's Seul-a going to get there?
Is she going alone?

488
00:40:39,568 --> 00:40:41,779
Or should I give her a ride too?

489
00:40:45,658 --> 00:40:46,659
Eyes on me.

490
00:40:47,284 --> 00:40:48,285
Eyes on you.

491
00:40:52,081 --> 00:40:53,165
Eyes on you.

492
00:40:53,582 --> 00:40:55,668
Thank you for calling Fan Goods Shop.

493
00:40:56,794 --> 00:40:58,712
Yes. The slogan?

494
00:40:59,380 --> 00:41:02,091
"Take my wallet, Hun-i."

495
00:41:02,174 --> 00:41:04,426
We're currently sold out.

496
00:41:04,510 --> 00:41:07,137
"Min-i stole my heart"
will be available tomorrow.

497
00:41:07,513 --> 00:41:09,265
You want 150? Okay.

498
00:41:09,473 --> 00:41:10,850
Okay. Thank you.

499
00:41:10,933 --> 00:41:12,560
Of course. It won't take long.

500
00:41:12,977 --> 00:41:13,978
Bye.

501
00:41:14,520 --> 00:41:16,063
One, two, three.

502
00:41:16,146 --> 00:41:17,815
One, two.

503
00:41:24,613 --> 00:41:27,283
- Okay.
- Nice. Good job.

504
00:41:35,249 --> 00:41:37,209
REUNION OF D.N.X
IN A FULL GROUP COMEBACK

505
00:41:40,170 --> 00:41:41,547
Oh, my gosh!

506
00:42:03,652 --> 00:42:06,196
Now, attention!

507
00:42:07,281 --> 00:42:08,365
You know what I'm going to do.

508
00:42:09,325 --> 00:42:11,035
It's time.

509
00:42:11,994 --> 00:42:12,995
Okay.

510
00:42:13,412 --> 00:42:16,332
There's something

511
00:42:16,582 --> 00:42:18,250
all new recruits must go through.

512
00:42:18,876 --> 00:42:20,836
Chae-yeon, are you

513
00:42:21,170 --> 00:42:24,048
Team Ha-gi or Team Chan?

514
00:42:24,131 --> 00:42:25,174
Or Team Jin-sang?

515
00:42:28,385 --> 00:42:31,513
- There must be at least one...
- Quiet.

516
00:42:33,265 --> 00:42:34,934
I'm on Team...

517
00:42:45,527 --> 00:42:46,570
Ha-gi.

518
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:53,077
You should've chosen Team Jin-sang.

519
00:42:53,494 --> 00:42:56,163
She used to be on Team Ha-gi too.

520
00:42:57,206 --> 00:43:00,417
- I'm on Team Young-woo now.
- I'm on Team Min-a.

521
00:43:00,501 --> 00:43:02,336
Didn't I tell you not to flaunt
your office romance?

522
00:43:02,419 --> 00:43:03,587
Stop it.

523
00:43:03,963 --> 00:43:07,341
By the way, is Mr. Kang single?

524
00:43:12,096 --> 00:43:13,263
Yes.

525
00:43:13,347 --> 00:43:16,392
Separate the preferred brand data
for North America and Europe.

526
00:43:34,618 --> 00:43:37,997
It looks like he's doing nothing,
but working.

527
00:43:38,747 --> 00:43:39,790
Okay.

528
00:43:40,666 --> 00:43:42,042
Do you want me to tell you?

529
00:43:42,126 --> 00:43:44,962
Whether Mr. Kang is
in a relationship or not?

530
00:43:46,755 --> 00:43:48,465
Oh, I'm sorry.

531
00:43:49,758 --> 00:43:52,302
- I knew it.
- Too bad.

532
00:43:52,928 --> 00:43:54,013
He already has a girlfriend.

533
00:43:56,932 --> 00:43:58,517
Da-reum!

534
00:44:00,352 --> 00:44:03,105
I, Nam Da-reum, just landed.

535
00:44:09,319 --> 00:44:10,571
Really?

536
00:44:23,292 --> 00:44:25,711
Welcome back. When did you come back?

537
00:44:30,549 --> 00:44:31,592
I thought you were coming tomorrow.

538
00:44:32,384 --> 00:44:33,469
I moved it up a day.

539
00:44:34,928 --> 00:44:35,929
Why?

540
00:44:38,432 --> 00:44:39,433
Because I missed you.

541
00:45:08,462 --> 00:45:10,047
I'm finally home.

542
00:45:14,802 --> 00:45:16,095
There's something
we haven't done yet.

543
00:45:31,527 --> 00:45:32,903
This is it.

544
00:45:35,614 --> 00:45:37,616
The reason I wanted to be back.

545
00:45:58,971 --> 00:46:01,265
The manager in charge will
suggest the merchandise

546
00:46:01,348 --> 00:46:03,225
in time for your comeback.

547
00:46:03,600 --> 00:46:04,935
Who's the new manager?

548
00:46:09,773 --> 00:46:11,024
Hello.

549
00:46:11,108 --> 00:46:13,360
- Hello.
- Hello.

550
00:46:16,613 --> 00:46:20,242
I'm your D.N.X collaboration
project manager, Nam Da-reum.

551
00:46:20,325 --> 00:46:21,493
Nice to meet you.

552
00:46:24,913 --> 00:46:26,957
We're honored to have you.

553
00:46:27,583 --> 00:46:29,126
Then let me begin.

554
00:46:30,711 --> 00:46:34,047
Your fan song "YOU" is the motive
of this collaboration.

555
00:46:34,131 --> 00:46:36,550
I reflected your gratitude
to your fans for waiting so long

556
00:46:36,633 --> 00:46:38,177
in the merchandise.

557
00:46:38,552 --> 00:46:41,847
As you can see,
I prepared three items.

558
00:46:41,930 --> 00:46:43,891
A T-shirt, a tote bag, and a cap.

559
00:46:44,224 --> 00:46:47,102
You can see the details
on the T-shirt.

560
00:46:47,311 --> 00:46:50,147
The pocket on the left
that's close to the heart is

561
00:46:50,230 --> 00:46:53,942
embroidered with lyrics from "YOU."

562
00:46:54,151 --> 00:46:55,611
That was good.

563
00:46:57,988 --> 00:46:59,031
That was cool.

564
00:46:59,114 --> 00:47:01,450
Oh, you're teasing me.

565
00:47:01,992 --> 00:47:03,202
I mean it.

566
00:47:04,453 --> 00:47:06,121
We're working together for real now.

567
00:47:06,872 --> 00:47:08,290
So I'd better pull this off.

568
00:47:08,874 --> 00:47:11,043
I'm not going to handle this project
as a fan.

569
00:47:11,335 --> 00:47:14,004
- Then?
- As a manager

570
00:47:14,087 --> 00:47:15,380
who understands the fans.

571
00:47:17,299 --> 00:47:18,759
I look forward to working with you

572
00:47:19,259 --> 00:47:20,969
Manager Nam Da-reum.

573
00:47:25,724 --> 00:47:29,394
- Likewise, Artist Lee Chan.
- Thank you.

574
00:47:32,397 --> 00:47:33,899
Good luck.

575
00:47:42,574 --> 00:47:44,576
That was a good briefing.

576
00:47:46,370 --> 00:47:49,206
- Did you hear it?
- I could hear your voice outside.

577
00:47:49,706 --> 00:47:50,958
You sounded pretty confident.

578
00:47:52,376 --> 00:47:54,002
I can leave you
with an even bigger project now.

579
00:47:55,337 --> 00:47:57,798
Are you complimenting me,
so you can make me work overtime?

580
00:47:58,840 --> 00:47:59,883
Not today.

581
00:48:01,051 --> 00:48:03,470
- Why not?
- I have a date with my boyfriend.

582
00:48:18,277 --> 00:48:19,528
THROUGH ALL TIME AND SPACE

583
00:48:19,611 --> 00:48:21,363
For the lyrics,
the fans will like this...

584
00:48:23,907 --> 00:48:25,575
and this the most.

585
00:48:25,659 --> 00:48:26,743
Okay, Ms. Da-reum.

586
00:48:27,244 --> 00:48:28,704
Then...

587
00:48:29,663 --> 00:48:31,415
Is this right?

588
00:48:33,208 --> 00:48:34,209
That's perfect.

589
00:48:37,337 --> 00:48:39,006
D.N.X CONCERT ATTIRE REFERENCE DESIGN

590
00:48:43,135 --> 00:48:44,594
CHECK COMEBACK SHOWCASE SPONSOR BOOTH

591
00:48:44,678 --> 00:48:46,555
CONFIRM STAGE OUTFIT KEY MERCHANDISE

592
00:48:46,763 --> 00:48:48,557
This is the hardest.

593
00:48:56,523 --> 00:48:57,649
MANAGER NA WON-BIN

594
00:48:58,608 --> 00:48:59,776
Yes, Mr. Na.

595
00:49:02,362 --> 00:49:03,363
What?

596
00:49:05,449 --> 00:49:09,286
Someone posted
a terrorist threat online.

597
00:49:09,494 --> 00:49:11,204
It's likely to be a prank

598
00:49:11,621 --> 00:49:13,957
but the police are going
to search the whole area.

599
00:49:14,541 --> 00:49:15,959
So we had to cancel the venue.

600
00:49:17,627 --> 00:49:20,881
So the place we booked in a rush is

601
00:49:21,882 --> 00:49:23,050
here.

602
00:49:23,133 --> 00:49:24,134
CONCERT HALL

603
00:49:27,637 --> 00:49:28,805
Isn't it too small?

604
00:49:28,889 --> 00:49:30,390
The stage is too close
to the audience.

605
00:49:31,767 --> 00:49:34,102
So we'll have to change
the stage outfit.

606
00:49:35,854 --> 00:49:38,523
- Our key merchandise too?
- Sorry about that.

607
00:49:39,274 --> 00:49:41,610
I'll have to ask you to change it
according to their new stage outfit.

608
00:50:26,655 --> 00:50:29,116
<i>Announce the change of address
on all available channels.</i>

609
00:50:32,744 --> 00:50:34,121
CHANGE IN SHOWCASE VENUE

610
00:50:35,789 --> 00:50:37,040
Let me check.

611
00:50:37,457 --> 00:50:39,709
Show only the half
of the merchandise shelf.

612
00:50:40,293 --> 00:50:43,171
<i>Since it's invitation only,
create a registration link.</i>

613
00:50:46,383 --> 00:50:47,384
{\an8}1ST D.N.X FANDOM PRESIDENT

614
00:50:47,467 --> 00:50:49,803
My blood is finally pumping again.

615
00:50:51,680 --> 00:50:53,265
<i>Pay attention, D-Angels.</i>

616
00:50:53,348 --> 00:50:55,225
{\an8}<i>This is where D.N.X is performing
for real.</i>

617
00:50:55,600 --> 00:50:56,852
<i>Check the link and run for it.</i>

618
00:51:04,734 --> 00:51:05,986
1ST D.N.X FANDOM PRESIDENT
CHECK THE LINK

619
00:51:06,069 --> 00:51:07,154
THE WHOLE GROUP? FOR REAL?
I'M IN TEARS

620
00:51:16,204 --> 00:51:18,123
SATURDAY, OCTOBER 3, 2026
ART LIVE HALL

621
00:51:29,259 --> 00:51:30,886
Enjoy cheering.

622
00:51:31,178 --> 00:51:33,555
Hello, take one.

623
00:51:33,638 --> 00:51:35,307
- Enjoy cheering.
- Good luck.

624
00:51:35,390 --> 00:51:36,516
Thank you.

625
00:51:36,600 --> 00:51:38,643
- Hello. Take one.
- Enjoy cheering.

626
00:51:38,727 --> 00:51:40,604
- Check if that's you.
- Did you make that yourself?

627
00:51:40,687 --> 00:51:41,938
- Yes.
- Nice.

628
00:51:42,022 --> 00:51:43,523
- That's so cool.
- Thank you.

629
00:51:44,024 --> 00:51:45,275
President Kim!

630
00:51:46,234 --> 00:51:47,360
I was waiting for your post!

631
00:51:47,444 --> 00:51:48,945
- I read your posting.
- Really?

632
00:51:49,029 --> 00:51:50,489
- Did you read my post?
- Yes.

633
00:51:50,572 --> 00:51:51,573
Awesome.

634
00:51:51,656 --> 00:51:53,074
Here. Take one.

635
00:51:53,158 --> 00:51:54,659
- Thank you.
- We'll be cheering inside.

636
00:52:00,832 --> 00:52:01,833
All right.

637
00:52:02,250 --> 00:52:04,503
Lastly, you need to put
on the merchandise from Appello.

638
00:52:07,130 --> 00:52:08,173
Hello.

639
00:52:08,256 --> 00:52:10,383
- Hello.
- Good to see you again.

640
00:52:17,724 --> 00:52:18,850
Ta-da.

641
00:52:27,901 --> 00:52:29,694
That's nice.
That looks like a shooting star.

642
00:52:30,028 --> 00:52:31,821
- Is that...
- Yes.

643
00:52:32,989 --> 00:52:34,950
The stage is smaller.

644
00:52:35,033 --> 00:52:36,868
but the fans will be happy
to get closer to you.

645
00:52:38,245 --> 00:52:41,248
So I just added small details.

646
00:52:42,916 --> 00:52:44,918
The closest light you can see.

647
00:52:57,556 --> 00:52:58,598
Thank you

648
00:52:59,266 --> 00:53:00,809
for giving this back to me.

649
00:53:05,021 --> 00:53:07,440
It's time for you
to shine on stage now.

650
00:53:11,403 --> 00:53:12,404
Sounds good.

651
00:53:22,872 --> 00:53:23,999
Are you ready?

652
00:53:27,335 --> 00:53:29,379
What about the fans? Are there many?

653
00:53:31,756 --> 00:53:32,841
See it for yourself.

654
00:53:35,677 --> 00:53:37,470
It's worth coming all the way here.

655
00:53:37,554 --> 00:53:39,306
I get to see them in front.

656
00:53:39,389 --> 00:53:40,807
Gosh, I'm so nervous.

657
00:53:40,890 --> 00:53:42,350
I hope Roy does well.

658
00:53:46,271 --> 00:53:47,272
I believe

659
00:53:48,106 --> 00:53:49,274
in the stage genius.

660
00:53:49,357 --> 00:53:50,483
The stage master!

661
00:53:51,443 --> 00:53:52,485
I know Roy can do it.

662
00:53:55,280 --> 00:53:56,740
Who's your favorite, Mi-mi?

663
00:53:57,240 --> 00:53:59,826
I first began as Chan.

664
00:54:00,201 --> 00:54:02,454
Then I became obsessed with Hyeok.

665
00:54:03,580 --> 00:54:04,664
What about now?

666
00:54:05,415 --> 00:54:06,416
You?

667
00:54:09,002 --> 00:54:10,170
That's all that matters.

668
00:54:11,296 --> 00:54:12,339
Hey!

669
00:54:14,132 --> 00:54:15,342
Get a room, will you?

670
00:54:16,885 --> 00:54:17,886
Today

671
00:54:19,137 --> 00:54:21,306
my bias is returning to the stage.

672
00:54:21,806 --> 00:54:22,974
It should be a national holiday.

673
00:54:24,184 --> 00:54:25,226
Wait.

674
00:54:25,727 --> 00:54:26,811
Let's go.

675
00:54:32,525 --> 00:54:34,986
Okay, they waited nine years for us.

676
00:54:35,779 --> 00:54:37,447
- Let's give our all.
- Okay.

677
00:54:41,534 --> 00:54:43,078
- One.
- Two.

678
00:54:43,161 --> 00:54:44,496
- Three.
- Four.

679
00:54:44,829 --> 00:54:46,498
Five. Let's go.

680
00:54:46,581 --> 00:54:48,166
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

681
00:55:13,108 --> 00:55:14,734
- Get in the picture.
- Okay.

682
00:55:14,818 --> 00:55:17,028
One, two, three.

683
00:55:39,968 --> 00:55:41,219
They're here!

684
00:56:14,085 --> 00:56:15,837
Hyeok!

685
00:56:16,045 --> 00:56:17,756
Hyeok!

686
00:56:17,839 --> 00:56:18,965
So cool!

687
00:56:25,430 --> 00:56:31,019
- D.N.X!
- D.N.X!

688
00:56:33,897 --> 00:56:35,315
I love them.

689
00:56:35,398 --> 00:56:41,362
- D.N.X!
- D.N.X!

690
00:56:44,783 --> 00:56:45,784
Well...

691
00:56:46,451 --> 00:56:49,454
We weren't sure what to sing
for our first song.

692
00:56:50,205 --> 00:56:51,247
But first

693
00:56:51,623 --> 00:56:55,001
thank you so much for waiting for us
for all these years.

694
00:57:03,092 --> 00:57:04,177
This song is...

695
00:57:10,517 --> 00:57:11,726
dedicated to you and everyone...

696
00:57:12,519 --> 00:57:14,604
who helped us...

697
00:57:16,189 --> 00:57:17,816
get back on stage.

698
00:57:22,654 --> 00:57:23,738
The title is...

699
00:57:26,449 --> 00:57:27,450
"YOU."

700
00:57:45,385 --> 00:57:49,973
<i>Perhaps everything that shines</i>

701
00:57:50,056 --> 00:57:54,060
<i>Fades away every day</i>

702
00:57:54,143 --> 00:57:58,481
<i>Dreaming makes me feel like myself</i>

703
00:57:58,565 --> 00:58:02,819
<i>But now,
I'm barely surviving each day</i>

704
00:58:02,902 --> 00:58:07,282
<i>The attention that surrounds me</i>

705
00:58:07,365 --> 00:58:11,953
<i>And waiting for the cheers</i>

706
00:58:12,036 --> 00:58:16,165
<i>Makes me nervous
like walking on thin ice</i>

707
00:58:16,249 --> 00:58:19,502
<i>I close my eyes and dream</i>

708
00:58:19,586 --> 00:58:20,712
<i>- Goodnight</i>
<i>- </i>Chan.

709
00:58:20,795 --> 00:58:24,007
<i>Sometimes everything brings me</i>

710
00:58:25,842 --> 00:58:28,803
<i>Down</i>

711
00:58:29,804 --> 00:58:32,140
<i>Only you</i>

712
00:58:32,223 --> 00:58:36,686
<i>Only you make me feel like I exist</i>

713
00:58:37,145 --> 00:58:38,271
So cool!

714
00:58:38,897 --> 00:58:42,942
<i>When I get lost</i>

715
00:58:43,026 --> 00:58:47,113
<i>In the world</i>

716
00:58:47,864 --> 00:58:49,532
<i>Through all time</i>

717
00:58:49,616 --> 00:58:52,827
- <i>And space</i>
- Hyeok!

718
00:58:52,911 --> 00:58:57,248
<i>We'll dream together again</i>

719
00:58:58,875 --> 00:59:03,129
<i>Only you</i>

720
00:59:03,212 --> 00:59:06,090
<i>Make me feel like I exist</i>

721
00:59:12,055 --> 00:59:14,682
{\an8}BACK AS FIVE AGAIN
D-ANGEL WILL BE WITH YOU FOREVER

722
00:59:14,766 --> 00:59:16,684
SHINING STARS ON STAGE
D.N.X FOREVER

723
00:59:23,399 --> 00:59:27,445
<i>It's surprising</i>

724
00:59:27,820 --> 00:59:31,032
<i>How time changes everything</i>

725
00:59:31,115 --> 00:59:32,283
Roy!

726
00:59:32,367 --> 00:59:36,079
<i>We were nothing at first</i>

727
00:59:37,330 --> 00:59:38,623
<i>I once</i>

728
00:59:38,915 --> 00:59:40,833
<i>chased after a shining star.</i>

729
00:59:46,297 --> 00:59:48,508
<i>But what lit my path</i>

730
00:59:49,384 --> 00:59:50,718
<i>was more than that.</i>

731
00:59:53,763 --> 00:59:55,848
<i>Every time I thought I was alone</i>

732
00:59:56,599 --> 00:59:59,310
<i>there was a light shining beside me.</i>

733
00:59:59,519 --> 01:00:04,023
I think I like you, Mr. Kang.

734
01:00:07,443 --> 01:00:09,112
<i>No matter how hard things get</i>

735
01:00:10,446 --> 01:00:11,614
<i>don't let go of my hand.</i>

736
01:00:15,743 --> 01:00:16,828
<i>But now</i>

737
01:00:17,620 --> 01:00:18,621
<i>I know...</i>

738
01:00:21,749 --> 01:00:23,459
<i>that stars are not far away.</i>

739
01:00:26,004 --> 01:00:27,714
<i>All these lights are</i>

740
01:00:28,631 --> 01:00:33,136
<i>stars emitting their own light
from where they are.</i>

741
01:00:34,929 --> 01:00:36,973
<i>Only you</i>

742
01:00:37,056 --> 01:00:42,228
<i>Only you make me feel like I exist</i>

743
01:00:43,604 --> 01:00:45,940
<i>When I get lost</i>

744
01:00:46,024 --> 01:00:51,529
<i>In the world</i>

745
01:00:52,864 --> 01:00:57,535
<i>Through all time and space</i>

746
01:00:57,618 --> 01:01:02,123
<i>We'll dream together again</i>

747
01:01:03,583 --> 01:01:07,920
<i>Only you</i>

748
01:01:08,004 --> 01:01:10,882
<i>Make me feel like I exist</i>

749
01:01:28,191 --> 01:01:30,359
<i>The moment
I become someone's light...</i>

750
01:01:34,113 --> 01:01:35,239
<i>I, too</i>

751
01:01:36,491 --> 01:01:37,533
<i>start shining in my own way.</i>

752
01:01:58,721 --> 01:01:59,931
Over here.

753
01:02:02,558 --> 01:02:04,310
Oh, bubbles.

754
01:02:11,567 --> 01:02:12,568
Da-reum.

755
01:02:17,281 --> 01:02:18,282
It's so cute.

756
01:02:21,994 --> 01:02:24,205
- Do you like it?
- I love it.

757
01:02:25,873 --> 01:02:27,917
Get me a ring and make it a full set.

758
01:02:30,670 --> 01:02:31,671
No.

759
01:02:33,422 --> 01:02:34,632
It withers soon.

760
01:02:35,466 --> 01:02:37,343
But it feels good.

761
01:02:37,426 --> 01:02:40,054
Get me a ring with a big flower.

762
01:02:40,596 --> 01:02:41,681
Where are the flowers?

763
01:02:43,808 --> 01:02:46,310
But I want to give you this.

764
01:02:57,196 --> 01:02:58,197
I want

765
01:02:59,282 --> 01:03:00,366
to be a place

766
01:03:01,534 --> 01:03:03,286
for you to return to every day.

767
01:03:06,455 --> 01:03:07,498
Will you...

768
01:03:11,961 --> 01:03:13,004
stay by my side?

769
01:03:24,724 --> 01:03:25,725
Yes.

770
01:03:32,440 --> 01:03:34,942
I'll be by your side every day.

771
01:04:32,250 --> 01:04:36,170
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

